>No, you don't need them. But the Wizard may choose to steal them; so
>if you have any quest artifact that you want to keep, the invocation
>artifacts may distract the Wizard from that artifact. Not sure whether
>he prefers The Amulet to those invocation artifacts, but if not you'll
>have some stochastic advantage if you keep them, again to distract him.

Monsters with an AD_SAMU attack will pick items in the following
descending order of priority:
* The first object in your inventory linked list that looks like the
  Amulet of Yendor, except that the Wizard will never steal a fake, and
  nobody will steal a fake from you if you aren't carrying the real
  thing.
* Your quest artifact.
* The first bell of any description in your inventory linked list,
  except that the Wizard will never steal a bell that is not the Bell
  of Opening, and no amulet thief will steal an ordinary bell if you
  do not have the Bell of Opening.
* The Book of the Dead
* The Candelabrum of Invocation
